1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,746 --> 00:00:45,973
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:48,306
=Episode 17=

4
00:01:05,910 --> 00:01:06,669
Your Majesty.

5
00:01:07,190 --> 00:01:08,669
My sister is still next door.

6
00:01:10,630 --> 00:01:11,910
When I look at you,

7
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:14,869
I see Roujia as she once was.

8
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:18,190
You're both mine.

9
00:01:18,910 --> 00:01:19,830
Both of you.

10
00:01:55,069 --> 00:01:56,349
(Everyone thought)

11
00:01:56,709 --> 00:01:58,750
(His Majesty loved only the Empress.)

12
00:01:59,309 --> 00:02:00,390
(But in the end,)

13
00:02:00,709 --> 00:02:02,869
(he was the first to betray her.)

14
00:02:17,110 --> 00:02:17,749
Your Highness.

15
00:02:19,629 --> 00:02:20,429
Get out!

16
00:02:29,589 --> 00:02:30,390
Your Majesty.

17
00:02:31,909 --> 00:02:33,350
You said it yourself.

18
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:36,550
I was the one most like her.

19
00:02:44,469 --> 00:02:46,029
I understood you best.

20
00:02:46,709 --> 00:02:48,230
So why...

21
00:02:49,589 --> 00:02:51,629
why are you holding her like this?

22
00:02:52,469 --> 00:02:54,510
Why are you saying to her

23
00:02:54,869 --> 00:02:56,309
the things you once said to me?

24
00:03:03,709 --> 00:03:04,830
Could it be...

25
00:03:05,429 --> 00:03:07,270
that I'm getting old?

26
00:03:12,350 --> 00:03:13,909
(What you stole)

27
00:03:15,110 --> 00:03:16,790
(was never truly yours.)

28
00:03:18,790 --> 00:03:20,909
(You lost.)

29
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:31,480
(Treasures of Heaven and Earth)

30
00:03:37,309 --> 00:03:39,189
Noble Lady Hui, why did you ask me

31
00:03:39,189 --> 00:03:40,230
to come here today?

32
00:03:41,149 --> 00:03:43,589
His Majesty asked me
to help oversee palace affairs.

33
00:03:44,070 --> 00:03:45,709
There's still much I don't understand.

34
00:03:46,110 --> 00:03:47,510
I'd like to ask for your guidance.

35
00:03:48,110 --> 00:03:49,189
You're too kind.

36
00:03:49,909 --> 00:03:51,469
The hardest thing in this palace

37
00:03:51,790 --> 00:03:52,830
isn't managing affairs.

38
00:03:53,270 --> 00:03:54,110
It's reading people.

39
00:03:54,990 --> 00:03:56,589
Who to keep close,

40
00:03:56,869 --> 00:03:58,230
and who to keep at a distance.

41
00:03:58,749 --> 00:03:59,950
One wrong choice,

42
00:04:00,589 --> 00:04:02,309
and you'll end up like Consort Shu.

43
00:04:04,309 --> 00:04:05,790
Consort Shu was simply unfortunate.

44
00:04:06,270 --> 00:04:07,429
I feel sorry for her too.

45
00:04:08,070 --> 00:04:08,869
Unfortunate?

46
00:04:10,070 --> 00:04:11,230
I think

47
00:04:11,629 --> 00:04:13,270
she chose the wrong side.

48
00:04:13,869 --> 00:04:14,909
I'm afraid I'm too dull

49
00:04:15,350 --> 00:04:16,830
to follow you.

50
00:04:20,990 --> 00:04:21,990
Then surely

51
00:04:22,269 --> 00:04:23,550
you understand this, right?

52
00:04:25,670 --> 00:04:27,030
If His Majesty learned

53
00:04:27,030 --> 00:04:28,749
you had a lover outside the palace,

54
00:04:29,389 --> 00:04:30,509
what do you think he'd do?

55
00:04:35,429 --> 00:04:36,629
I only kept close to Consort Chen

56
00:04:37,189 --> 00:04:38,710
to protect myself in the palace.

57
00:04:39,189 --> 00:04:40,470
Please spare San.

58
00:04:40,670 --> 00:04:42,110
I'll do whatever you ask.

59
00:04:56,350 --> 00:04:57,069
Congratulations, Your Majesty.

60
00:04:57,069 --> 00:04:57,749
Congratulations, Your Highness.

61
00:04:57,869 --> 00:04:59,710
Noble Lady Hui has a pregnancy pulse.

62
00:05:06,030 --> 00:05:07,110
Wonderful, Su.

63
00:05:07,550 --> 00:05:08,790
We're finally going to have a child.

64
00:05:09,230 --> 00:05:09,629
Mm.

65
00:05:11,110 --> 00:05:11,749
Wonderful.

66
00:05:13,269 --> 00:05:14,030
Wonderful.

67
00:05:15,269 --> 00:05:16,110
Issue my decree.

68
00:05:16,550 --> 00:05:17,869
Promote Noble Lady Hui at once

69
00:05:18,350 --> 00:05:19,350
to Concubine Hui.

70
00:05:22,629 --> 00:05:23,269
Don't move.

71
00:05:24,629 --> 00:05:25,509
I...

72
00:05:25,990 --> 00:05:27,110
I'm deeply grateful, Your Majesty.

73
00:05:28,470 --> 00:05:28,790
Mm.

74
00:05:43,629 --> 00:05:44,470
Wanniang.

75
00:05:45,350 --> 00:05:45,990
This medicine...

76
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:48,350
can mimic a pregnancy pulse,

77
00:05:48,749 --> 00:05:50,509
but it's very hard on your body.

78
00:05:51,309 --> 00:05:53,230
It's only a little physical pain.

79
00:05:53,670 --> 00:05:55,230
Compared to what Shouhe endured,

80
00:05:56,309 --> 00:05:57,429
this is nothing.

81
00:05:59,350 --> 00:06:00,189
Tell Concubine De.

82
00:06:00,670 --> 00:06:01,550
It's time to act.

83
00:06:01,910 --> 00:06:02,470
Okay.

84
00:06:03,670 --> 00:06:04,230
That wretch!

85
00:06:04,790 --> 00:06:07,150
I've been with His Majesty three years

86
00:06:07,749 --> 00:06:08,829
and still have no child.

87
00:06:09,509 --> 00:06:11,470
She's been here only two months.

88
00:06:11,790 --> 00:06:13,030
How can she already carry his child?

89
00:06:13,550 --> 00:06:14,509
Please calm down, Your Highness.

90
00:06:15,110 --> 00:06:15,670
Your Highness.

91
00:06:16,189 --> 00:06:18,590
His Majesty only favors her
because she's new.

92
00:06:19,150 --> 00:06:20,030
After all,

93
00:06:20,389 --> 00:06:22,350
she's just an outsider and a temptress.

94
00:06:23,030 --> 00:06:25,230
But once she gives birth,

95
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:28,309
she'll secure her place in the palace.

96
00:06:29,509 --> 00:06:31,150
By then, Your Highness,

97
00:06:31,150 --> 00:06:32,429
it'll be much harder to act against her.

98
00:06:32,869 --> 00:06:33,829
Not a chance.

99
00:06:36,670 --> 00:06:38,309
I'll show her that

100
00:06:38,749 --> 00:06:40,069
a lowly weed from outside the palace

101
00:06:40,389 --> 00:06:42,350
has no right to bear
His Majesty's child.

102
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:49,053
(Treasures of Heaven and Earth)

103
00:06:49,150 --> 00:06:50,509
Did we weave it this way last time?

104
00:06:50,509 --> 00:06:50,949
Mm.

105
00:06:51,350 --> 00:06:52,749
I thought the last one had eyes.

106
00:06:53,670 --> 00:06:54,790
Can you even weave?

107
00:06:55,189 --> 00:06:57,030
I taught you for ages.

108
00:06:57,629 --> 00:06:58,790
You still couldn't learn.

109
00:06:59,230 --> 00:07:00,230
You're hopeless.

110
00:07:01,429 --> 00:07:02,230
From now on,

111
00:07:02,670 --> 00:07:04,230
you don't need to worry about anything.

112
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:06,309
Just focus on taking care of yourself.

113
00:07:07,230 --> 00:07:08,269
I'll take care of you

114
00:07:08,710 --> 00:07:09,869
and the baby.

115
00:07:11,829 --> 00:07:13,309
Hearing you say that, Che,

116
00:07:13,710 --> 00:07:14,869
the baby and I

117
00:07:15,150 --> 00:07:16,749
can finally rest easy.

118
00:07:21,470 --> 00:07:22,389
Let me see what you made.

119
00:07:43,790 --> 00:07:44,389
Your Majesty.

120
00:07:45,230 --> 00:07:45,790
Your Majesty!

121
00:07:46,429 --> 00:07:47,269
What's wrong, Your Majesty?

122
00:07:48,189 --> 00:07:48,990
I don't know.

123
00:07:51,350 --> 00:07:52,429
I'm just a little dizzy.

124
00:07:53,629 --> 00:07:54,550
And a little hot.

125
00:07:55,230 --> 00:07:55,990
I'll...

126
00:07:56,429 --> 00:07:57,550
get you some water.

127
00:08:13,710 --> 00:08:14,509
Your Majesty.

128
00:08:40,689 --> 00:08:44,876
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

129
00:08:45,010 --> 00:08:48,623
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

130
00:08:48,858 --> 00:08:51,457
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

131
00:08:51,494 --> 00:08:53,774
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

132
00:08:53,821 --> 00:08:57,650
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

133
00:08:58,052 --> 00:09:01,405
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

134
00:09:02,332 --> 00:09:05,845
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

135
00:09:06,345 --> 00:09:08,912
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

136
00:09:09,038 --> 00:09:11,071
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

137
00:09:11,138 --> 00:09:14,915
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

138
00:09:15,265 --> 00:09:19,598
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

139
00:09:19,821 --> 00:09:23,328
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

140
00:09:23,509 --> 00:09:26,362
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

141
00:09:26,429 --> 00:09:32,043
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

142
00:09:32,083 --> 00:09:35,097
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

143
00:09:35,138 --> 00:09:41,146
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

144
00:09:41,813 --> 00:09:48,768
♪The past has faded away♪

145
00:09:48,768 --> 00:09:52,800
♪The past has faded away♪
